{
  "info": {
    "name": "SimpleStackWatch — MCP",
    "description": "Public-safe sample for the read-only SimpleStackWatch MCP endpoint (stateless Streamable HTTP).\n\nSetup:\n1. Enable Dashboard__Mcp__Enabled and set Dashboard__Mcp__BearerToken privately (32–512 non-whitespace characters). Restart the dashboard. For local development use the private launch profile; for deployment use the private environment file.\n2. Import this collection into Postman. Set baseUrl to your dashboard address (no trailing slash). Set bearerToken in a private local environment or local variable value, not the shared collection value. Use HTTPS for remote servers and an approved source IP if Nginx allowlisting is configured. Never share or export real tokens or target IDs.\n3. Send Initialize, Initialized notification, Ping, List tools, Get overview and List targets in order. Inspect the returned tool content and set targetId privately to an exact configured ID. Then send Get target status and Get target history. To run the entire collection, configure targetId first. A configured target is required for these last two calls; an empty history is valid.\n4. Run Missing token and Invalid token with MCP enabled. Both should return 401 (disabled MCP returns 404). No cookie/session is required; a dashboard login cookie is not an MCP credential.\n\nAll positive requests inherit Bearer authentication. The initialization test retains the negotiated protocol version (not a secret). Tests handle JSON and SSE response bodies. If Postman displays SSE as a stream, wait for the response to close. The monitoring tools are read-only and do not trigger new polling or resource changes. See README.md for configuration and deployment. Do not run against systems you are not authorized to monitor.",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
  },
  "auth": {
    "type": "bearer",
    "bearer": [
      {
        "key": "token",
        "value": "{{bearerToken}}",
        "type": "string"
      }
    ]
  },
  "variable": [
    {
      "key": "baseUrl",
      "value": "http://localhost:5080",
      "type": "string",
      "description": "Dashboard base URL, without trailing slash."
    },
    {
      "key": "mcpPath",
      "value": "/api/mcp",
      "type": "string",
      "description": "MCP HTTP route."
    },
    {
      "key": "bearerToken",
      "value": "",
      "type": "string",
      "description": "Set privately; never export or commit the populated value."
    },
    {
      "key": "targetId",
      "value": "",
      "type": "string",
      "description": "Exact configured target ID from List targets. Set privately."
    },
    {
      "key": "historyLimit",
      "value": "50",
      "type": "string",
      "description": "Number of stored checks (1–200)."
    },
    {
      "key": "protocolVersion",
      "value": "2025-06-18",
      "type": "string",
      "description": "Requested MCP protocol version; updated after successful initialization."
    }
  ],
  "item": [
    {
      "name": "01 — Protocol",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "01 Initialize",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json",
                "type": "text"
              },
              {
                "key": "Accept",
                "value": "application/json, text/event-stream",
                "type": "text"
              }
            ],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"jsonrpc\": \"2.0\",\n  \"id\": 1,\n  \"method\": \"initialize\",\n  \"params\": {\n    \"protocolVersion\": \"{{protocolVersion}}\",\n    \"capabilities\": {},\n    \"clientInfo\": {\n      \"name\": \"SimpleStackWatch Postman\",\n      \"version\": \"1.0.0\"\n    }\n  }\n}",
              "options": {
                "raw": {
                  "language": "json"
                }
              }
            },
            "url": "{{baseUrl}}{{mcpPath}}",
            "description": "Run first. Requests the same MCP version used by the application integration tests. The server may negotiate another supported version; the test saves only that non-secret protocol version."
          },
          "response": [],
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test(\"HTTP 200\", () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "const contentType = pm.response.headers.get(\"Content-Type\") || \"\";",
                  "const raw = pm.response.text();",
                  "const request = JSON.parse(pm.variables.replaceIn(pm.request.body.raw));",
                  "let message;",
                  "if (/text\\/event-stream/i.test(contentType)) {",
                  "    const events = raw.replace(/\\r\\n/g, \"\\n\").split(/\\n\\n/);",
                  "    for (const event of events) {",
                  "        const data = event.split(\"\\n\").filter(line => line.startsWith(\"data:\"))",
                  "            .map(line => line.slice(5).replace(/^ /, \"\")).join(\"\\n\");",
                  "        if (!data) continue;",
                  "        let candidate;",
                  "        try { candidate = JSON.parse(data); } catch (_) { continue; }",
                  "        if (candidate && candidate.id === request.id) { message = candidate; break; }",
                  "    }",
                  "} else if (/application\\/json/i.test(contentType)) {",
                  "    try { message = JSON.parse(raw); } catch (_) { /* assertion below reports failure */ }",
                  "}",
                  "pm.test(\"Matching JSON-RPC success response\", () => {",
                  "    pm.expect(message, \"Expected a JSON or SSE JSON-RPC reply\").to.be.an(\"object\");",
                  "    pm.expect(message.jsonrpc).to.equal(\"2.0\");",
                  "    pm.expect(message.id).to.equal(request.id);",
                  "    pm.expect(message).not.to.have.property(\"error\");",
                  "    pm.expect(message).to.have.property(\"result\");",
                  "});",
                  "pm.test(\"Server negotiated protocol and advertises tools\", () => {",
                  "    pm.expect(message.result.protocolVersion).to.be.a(\"string\").and.not.empty;",
                  "    pm.expect(message.result.serverInfo.name).to.be.a(\"string\");",
                  "    pm.expect(message.result.capabilities).to.have.property(\"tools\");",
                  "    pm.collectionVariables.set(\"protocolVersion\", message.result.protocolVersion);",
                  "});"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
